# Real configuration and key material never belong in the repository.
.env
# .env.stt holds the dictation service's own channel secret. A separate file exists
# precisely so the two services do not share an environment (STT/SECURITY-AUDIT.md
# finding 1) - which also means a .gitignore matching only ".env" does not cover it.
.env.stt
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.stt.example
certs/
!certs/.gitkeep
